    "tree_id": "cadb1818eaa392966647375aaa26ae34e8b9172b",
    "message": "fix(cloud): repair 429 key rotation sentinel handling\n\nThe rotation shipped in 69703e0 could not work. getNextOpenRouterKeyIndex\nsignals an exhausted pool with -1, a non-null Int, but the call site tested\n`next != null`. For a live key store that test is always true, so rotation\naccepted -1, re-read a blank key, and looped on the exhausted 429 forever.\n\nChanges:\n- CloudInferenceEngine: check `next >= 0`, and fall through to the normal\n  backoff when the pool is spent. A 429 on a single key can still clear\n  inside the retry window, and 503 always needs the backoff regardless of\n  key state, so terminating early would regress both.\n- SecureKeyStore: reject negative indices outright, and read the numbered\n  slots from BuildConfig. System.getenv is empty on Android, so the\n  env-var path was unreachable on-device.\n- build.gradle.kts: emit CLOUD_API_KEY_1..3 from EDGE_CLOUD_API_KEY_1..3.\n  Pool size is fixed at 3 so the BuildConfig fields stay static.\n- secrets.properties.example: document the spare keys.\n- OpenRouterKeyRotationTest: 4 tests pinning the sentinel contract, the\n  single-key case, and that a spent pool terminates instead of looping.\n\n156/156 unit tests pass, lint clean.",
    "timestamp": "2026-10-05T12:50:49Z",
